From 022bed29b7fb6380717169815696eac19bf66735 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hexagonrpcd: answer apps_std fopen_with_env_fd lookups

The SM8750 ADSP sensor domain calls apps_std method 36 shortly after it
has read its configuration, as an extended method (sc 0x1f050100: method
31, five input buffers, one output buffer, real ID in the first word).
In Qualcomm's apps_std IDL, as generated into the reference skel of
quic/fastrpc and matched by the stock libadsprpc.so dispatcher, method
36 is

  fopen_with_env_fd(in string envvarname, in string delim,
                    in string name, in string mode,
                    rout long fd, rout long len)

The reference listener searches the path in envvarname, reads the file
into an rpcmem buffer, maps that buffer into the DSP process and returns
the buffer's file descriptor and length; an absent file is answered with
the host errno ENOENT. hexagonrpcd has no method 36, so the listener
stops at the first such call.

Serve the lookup with the same search directories as fopen_with_env and
answer an absent file (or an unavailable search directory) with ENOENT,
as the reference does. Mapping a buffer into the DSP is not implemented,
so a present file is refused with AEE_EUNSUPPORTED and logged instead of
being served wrongly, and write or update modes are refused like in
fopen_with_env. Only the exact ROM scalar shape is accepted. The search
path selection moves into a helper shared with fopen_with_env, whose
results are unchanged.

Cover the wire encoding, absent and present files, file-number leaks,
refused modes, unknown variables, unterminated strings, other scalar
shapes and the unchanged fopen_with_env results with a host test.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
